Hi D.J.,

You might be able to find some information on the 'unmarked' google group.  Regarding the first question, if you have multiple visits to specific sites and the observer changes, observer can be specified as a yearlySiteCov. Otherwise, with a 'single-visit' design, variance in detection can only be measured at the site-level...there are no repeated observations. Regarding the second: https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/unmarked/vignettes/distsamp.pdf may be useful.

